WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.400
This is the Microsoft for Education Daily, for Saturday.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.180
Here's your day in Microsoft updates, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.680
Small wins. In Windows' Release Preview,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.450
a new pointer indicator helps students with low vision find the mouse.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.500
Hit Sticky Keys by accident? Turn it off right from the pop-up.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.280
For students, Narrator now reads maths aloud in 8 more languages,

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.800
from Greek and Polish to Vietnamese.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.980
Lights down for a video? Windows Hello can now briefly brighten your screen,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.730
so face sign-in still works.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:52.590
Teachers, files last saved in Word 2010 or earlier may reflow from December.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.940
Save a PDF first.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.770
Casting to the class screen? A Miracast fix stops it dropping resolution.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
For school IT,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.770
Release Preview lets hybrid joined PCs sign in with a security key, no password.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.920
And in the Beta channel,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.990
staff without admin rights can set their own BitLocker start-up PIN.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.000
University dev teams can now switch GitHub's AI code scanning on across repositories with a script,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:21.730
in preview.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.700
Running campus web apps? Azure Front Door Premium now checks client certificates,

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.880
and in preview, Entra tokens too.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.700
In Microsoft Research's latest roundup,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.270
a 31-year-old maths problem, the KLS conjecture, has been solved.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.500
A Microsoft researcher and a collaborator proved it,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.670
with AI exploring ideas while they steered the search.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.910
The fine print? Microsoft says it's deeply sorry for the outage that hit Outlook,

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.730
Teams, and schools worldwide.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.350
And after November's update, some Word documents may not print,

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.670
and KMS activation commands can fail.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.130
After hours, for Xbox's 25th,

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:08.650
claim a free Xbox green Minecraft skin until December 10.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.240
Flight Simulator pilots get four throwback liveries automatically,

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.230
even one for the hot air balloon.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.740
And Xbox Insiders can shuffle Home backgrounds,

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.170
and put the Guide on the left or right.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.440
Bumpy week? Find the pointer, save the PDF, then go play. Small wins.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Day after day, the updates keep stacking up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.620
Some of it's shipped. The rest is on its way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.720
This has been the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.
